 change are load-bearing consumers not called out.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc6efcb5cbf6012cf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC-1 / tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:execute + tests/interfaces/adapters.py:link","norm_id":"n2733d499385e6d7c","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author adds two Case rows with op='link' and inputs={'force': ...} and finds execute() has no link branch and adapter.link cannot return an Outcome or accept force"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the Approach/Testing section, add: extend `write_parity_contract.execute()` with an `op == \"link\"` branch and thread `force` into it, and widen `Adapter.link` (LibraryAdapter/CLIAdapter/MCPAdapter) to accept `force` and return an `Outcome` so a refusal is classifiable.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify that link_core resolves the code repo root via config.repo_root(repo_root) (not tracker_dir) and passes THAT to referencing_commits, mirroring close_precheck's code_root/tracker split.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["link_core today derives only `tracker = tracker_dir(repo_root)` (src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py:57) and never computes a code root","The close path deliberately separates the two: `code_root = str(config.repo_root(repo_root))` while tracker reads use `config.tracker_dir(repo_root)` (close_precheck._completion_precheck, lines 552 & 569), and passes code_root as the scan's repo_root arg (_check_work_landed line 177)","Plan quote: 'referencing_commits(ids, tracker, repo_root)' — repo_root here is the code root the close callers already pass, but the plan never says link_core must resolve it via config.repo_root rather than pass the tracker dir"],"finding":"The plan does not specify that link_core must resolve the CODE repo root (distinct from the tracker) before invoking referencing_commits, so the scan may run git against the wrong directory when the tracker is relocated outside the code checkout.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd780d57befe14c39","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 1–3; helper signature referencing_commits(ids, tracker, repo_root)","norm_id":"n4e83ead89ffd92a5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A store whose tracker lives outside the git checkout (REBAR_ROOT / relocated tracker): scanning `git -C <tracker>` finds no repo → returns None → every caused_by link is silently ALLOWED (rule never fires); or scans an unrelated repo → false refusal"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Approach step 2, note that link_core computes `code_root = str(config.repo_root(repo_root))` and calls `referencing_commits(accepted_ids, tracker, code_root)`, matching the close gate's code-vs-tracker root separation.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_c